WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.625
A system boundary is a practical agreement
about what is included in the assessment.

2
00:00:05.775 --> 00:00:09.957
Our vessel receives product materials and
a heating or cooling service,

3
00:00:10.107 --> 00:00:12.539
and transfers bulk solution downstream.

4
00:00:12.689 --> 00:00:15.889
The simplified diagram shows these
interfaces.

5
00:00:16.039 --> 00:00:20.497
It does not assert that the utility is
qualified by qualifying the vessel.

6
00:00:20.647 --> 00:00:24.914
Each interface needs an owner and a clear
connection to the evidence for

7
00:00:25.064 --> 00:00:27.347
the supplying or receiving system.

8
00:00:28.097 --> 00:00:31.574
A component does not need to touch product
to affect quality.

9
00:00:31.724 --> 00:00:35.073
A temperature sensor sends information to
a controller,

10
00:00:35.223 --> 00:00:38.850
which can influence the jacket service and
therefore the product.

11
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:43.736
Conversely, physical proximity alone does
not make every room object

12
00:00:43.886 --> 00:00:45.209
equally important.

13
00:00:45.359 --> 00:00:49.412
Describe the mechanism by which a
component failure could affect the

14
00:00:49.562 --> 00:00:50.653
process.

15
00:00:50.803 --> 00:00:55.475
Use that explanation to support scope
decisions rather than relying only

16
00:00:55.625 --> 00:00:57.566
on a label such as critical.

17
00:00:58.316 --> 00:01:01.666
Engineering understands the design and
installation.

18
00:01:01.816 --> 00:01:05.869
Operations understands how people use and
clean the equipment.

19
00:01:06.019 --> 00:01:10.606
Quality oversight connects decisions to
the pharmaceutical quality system.

20
00:01:10.756 --> 00:01:15.321
Additional expertise may be needed from
development, microbiology,

21
00:01:15.471 --> 00:01:18.202
metrology or information technology.

22
00:01:18.352 --> 00:01:21.530
This is a suggested team for the fictional
project,

23
00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:24.326
not a universal organizational chart.

24
00:01:24.476 --> 00:01:29.084
Identify who prepares evidence, who
reviews it and who has authority to

25
00:01:29.234 --> 00:01:30.706
approve each decision.

26
00:01:31.456 --> 00:01:34.549
Review this handover: the vessel report is
ready,

27
00:01:34.699 --> 00:01:39.008
but the transfer hose has no approved
cleaning procedure and the utility

28
00:01:39.158 --> 00:01:41.100
connection is not identified.

29
00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:46.007
Calling the vessel ready for routine use
would hide unresolved interfaces.

30
00:01:46.157 --> 00:01:48.482
Record the gaps and assess their impact.

31
00:01:48.632 --> 00:01:53.048
For the activity, draw a boundary and
assign an owner to each interface.

32
00:01:53.198 --> 00:01:58.977
A boundary is useful only when work
outside it has somewhere explicit to go.
